.TH plotcake 8  "2026-11-23" "USER COMMANDS"
.SH NAME
plotcake \- Plot curves in linux termimal.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plotcake
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]...

.B <stdout serial of numbers> | plotcake
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
plotcake is the tool of terminal curves plot.

This program is a basic command of Plotcake.

.SH REQUIREMENTS
ncurses, json-c

.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS
\fB\-\-axis-curve-type\fR [TYPE]
Plotting draw types for coordinate axes, the supported types will be listed or use --draws show all types supported.

.SS
\fB\-\-black-background\fR
The drawing uses a black background instead of a transparent one.

.SS
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-color\fR [COLOR]
Specify line colors, if an invalid value is entered, the supported line colors will be listed, can match color prefixes, such as 'r' matching 'red' (may be listed multiple times).

.SS
\fB\-\-delta\fR
Use delta value (shortcut 't': change numerical scaling type for paint).
If a stacked line chart is plotted, the 'delta' plot type will revert to the raw data.

.SS
\fB\-\-enable-stacked-line-chart\fR
Create a stacked line chart; this type of chart layers multiple data series on top of one another, illustrating both the "overall trend" and the "contribution of each individual series" (shortcut 's': enable/disable stacked line chart).

.SS
\fB\-\-exponential\fR
Use base-e exponential (shortcut 't': change numerical scaling type for paint)

.SS
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR [FILE]
Specify input file, the format must conform to the plotcake file format. You can run plotcake once to view the generated files (txt).

.SS
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR [TIME]
Specify interval time, the default unit is nanoseconds, but units such as 'min', 's', 'ms', 'us', and 'ns' can also be used. If data comes from stdin, this interval will limit the ploting rate.

.SS
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-legend\fR [LABEL]
Specify legend (may be listed multiple times)

.SS
\fB\-\-colors\fR
Show line colors for --color.

.SS
\fB\-\-logarithmic\fR
Use natural logarithmic (shortcut 't': change numerical scaling type for paint)

.SS
\fB\-\-logarithmic10\fR
Use base-10 logarithmic, the curve shape is exactly the same as --logarithmic, only the values of the tick labels on the axes are different (shortcut 't': change numerical scaling type for paint).

.SS
\fB\-\-draws\fR
Show draw types for --draw.

.SS
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-draw\fR [TYPE]
Specify draw types, if an invalid value is entered, the supported draw types will be listed or use --draws show all types supported (may be listed multiple times).

.SS
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-ram\fR
Display memory curves instead of loadavg.

.SS
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-ofile\fR [NAME]
Specify the output file name, excluding the extension.

.SS
\fB\-\-stdin-buffer-size\fR [BYTES]
Specify stdin buffer size to allocate.

.SS
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tmout\fR [TIME]
Specify timeout time, the default unit is nanoseconds, but units such as 'min', 's', 'ms', 'us', and 'ns' can also be used.

.SS
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR [TITLE]
Specify title name.

.SS
\fB\-\-vertical-plotting\fR [TITLE]
Generally, the x-axis is horizontal and the y-axis is vertical; when plotting in a vertical orientation, the axes are swapped.

.SS
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Turn on verbose mode.

.SS
\fB\-\-win-border\fR [utf8]
Sets the border type for the pop-up window; currently, only 'utf8' and 'auto' are supported.

.SS
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-xlabel\fR [LABEL]
Specify x axis label.

.SS
\fB\-\-x-index\fR
Use index as x axis value instead of timeval (shortcut: 'x': switch x axis type).

.SS
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-ylabel\fR [LABEL]
Specify y axis label.

.SS
\fB\-?\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help information.

.SS
\fB\-\-usage\fR
Give a short usage message.

.SS
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information.

.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Draw loadavg
\&
.\" SRC BEGIN (loadavg.sh)
.EX
$ plotcake
.EE
.\" SRC END

.SS Draw memory usage
\&
.\" SRC BEGIN (memory.sh)
.EX
$ plotcake -M
.EE
.\" SRC END

.SS Read data from stdin
\&
.\" SRC BEGIN (stdin.sh)
.EX
# Draw opened file number
$ while awk '{print $1}' /proc/sys/fs/file-nr; do
     sleep 0.5
  done | plotcake --title 'Opened File Number' -l 'opened'

# Draw one line
$ seq 1 1 10 | plotcake
# Draw ten line
$ seq -s ' ' 1 1 10 | plotcake

# Work with tmux
$ tmux new-session -d -s plotcake plotcake [options]
$ tmux attach-session -t plotcake
$ tmux detach-client -s plotcake # Anther terminal
.EE
.\" SRC END

.SH STDIN DATA FORMAT

.TS
allbox;
lbx lb lb lb
l l l l.
Type	Format	Parsing	Example
T{
.na
.nh
.BR "3 Lines"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3 \en 1 2 3 \en 1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "echo -e '1 2 3 \en 1 2 3 \en 1 2 3' | plotcake"
T}
T{
.na
.nh
.BR "3 Lines"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3 ; 1 2 3 \en 1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "echo -e '1 2 3 ; 1 2 3 \en 1 2 3' | plotcake"
T}
T{
.na
.nh
.BR "3 Lines"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3 ; 1 2 3 ; 1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
.br
.na
.nh
.BR "1 2 3"
T}	T{
.na
.nh
.BR "echo -e '1 2 3 ; 1 2 3 ; 1 2 3' | plotcake"
T}
.TE

